the only place this could have caused a XentMM is is **cookiep was
nonsense. If the resource pointer was NULL, you would have died in
rman_activate_resource.

I've found the 't' command in ddb to be fairly accurate, but perhaps not.
I didn't note the actual PC && RA- if I get a  chance later today to try
it again, I'll try and trace it more fully.

